A||||1||BENGAL4||BALANCER INSTALLATION
Z||000000||BENGAL4||07-28-99||09:36 PM||||I am having trouble getting the balancer back on. I tried the Haynes method of using a socket, washer and retaining bolt and it went on a little, but then the bolt became too hard to turn and I was afraid I would strip out the threads in the crank. The Haynes manual mentioned a GM installation tool, GM J-29113. Is this availible anywhere? Any other tricks or suggestions? This is my first time installing a timing set and I want to thank everyone for the advice. 
Z||000001||batboy||07-28-99||10:26 PM||||You might try removing the balancer again and screwing the bolt in and out to make sure the threads are ok, clean and lubricate the crank snout, then try it again. Make sure the crank key is seated properly and is going into the balancer slot ok too.
